	<!-- EN: Facial Animation Performance -->
	<FAPerf_SettingsCategory>Facial Animation Performance</FAPerf_SettingsCategory>
	<!-- EN: Status: active — Facial Animation is running with optimized code paths. -->
	<FAPerf_Status_Active>Status: active — Facial Animation is running with optimized code paths.</FAPerf_Status_Active>
	<!-- EN: Status: NOT active — Facial Animation is missing or an incompatible version was detected. It is running with its original code. See the log for details. -->
	<FAPerf_Status_Inactive>Status: NOT active — Facial Animation is missing or an incompatible version was detected. It is running with its original code. See the log for details.</FAPerf_Status_Inactive>
	<!-- EN: Skip fully hidden face layers when drawing -->
	<FAPerf_SkipHiddenLayers>Skip fully hidden face layers when drawing</FAPerf_SkipHiddenLayers>
	<!-- EN: Facial Animation submits invisible (fully transparent) draw calls for hidden face layers — up to ~18 per pawn when facing away from the camera. Skipping them is pixel-identical and saves CPU and GPU every frame.\n\nDisable only if a face addon renders incorrectly. -->
	<FAPerf_SkipHiddenLayers_Tip>Facial Animation submits invisible (fully transparent) draw calls for hidden face layers — up to ~18 per pawn when facing away from the camera. Skipping them is pixel-identical and saves CPU and GPU every frame.\n\nDisable only if a face addon renders incorrectly.</FAPerf_SkipHiddenLayers_Tip>
	<!-- EN: Allow cached rendering while facing away -->
	<FAPerf_NorthCache>Allow cached rendering while facing away</FAPerf_NorthCache>
	<!-- EN: When a standing pawn faces away from the camera (north), no face parts are visible, so RimWorld's cached pawn frame is pixel-identical to live rendering. Animation timers pause while the face is hidden — the same thing that already happens for off-screen pawns.\n\nDisable to force live rendering at all rotations. -->
	<FAPerf_NorthCache_Tip>When a standing pawn faces away from the camera (north), no face parts are visible, so RimWorld's cached pawn frame is pixel-identical to live rendering. Animation timers pause while the face is hidden — the same thing that already happens for off-screen pawns.\n\nDisable to force live rendering at all rotations.</FAPerf_NorthCache_Tip>
	<!-- EN: Use cached pawn rendering when zoomed out -->
	<FAPerf_FarZoomCache>Use cached pawn rendering when zoomed out</FAPerf_FarZoomCache>
	<!-- EN: Extra FPS beyond the 1:1 optimizations: when the camera is zoomed out past the threshold below, pawns are drawn from RimWorld's render cache — faces pause at that distance (they are only a few pixels tall there). Zooming back in resumes animation instantly, and colonist-bar portraits keep animating regardless.\n\nOff = strictly identical behavior to Facial Animation. -->
	<FAPerf_FarZoomCache_Tip>Extra FPS beyond the 1:1 optimizations: when the camera is zoomed out past the threshold below, pawns are drawn from RimWorld's render cache — faces pause at that distance (they are only a few pixels tall there). Zooming back in resumes animation instantly, and colonist-bar portraits keep animating regardless.\n\nOff = strictly identical behavior to Facial Animation.</FAPerf_FarZoomCache_Tip>
	<!-- EN: Zoom threshold -->
	<FAPerf_FarZoomThreshold>Zoom threshold</FAPerf_FarZoomThreshold>
	<!-- EN: Camera zoom level (root size) beyond which the render cache is allowed. 18 = as soon as RimWorld itself is willing to cache pawns (mid zoom-out). 60 = only at extreme zoom-out. Lower values give more FPS but pause faces at closer zoom. -->
	<FAPerf_FarZoomThreshold_Tip>Camera zoom level (root size) beyond which the render cache is allowed. 18 = as soon as RimWorld itself is willing to cache pawns (mid zoom-out). 60 = only at extreme zoom-out. Lower values give more FPS but pause faces at closer zoom.</FAPerf_FarZoomThreshold_Tip>
